{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Cgj4XUpGEFGFo4dViCS6t","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"*You stand before me — a simple, ancient door set into a stone wall. There is no handle. No hinges visible. Just a single keyhole, dark and deep, centered where a knob should be.*\n\n*The metal around the keyhole is worn smooth by centuries of fingers tracing its edges. Cold air breathes outward from the opening, carrying the faint scent of dust and something older — iron, perhaps, or time itself.*\n\n*I wait.*\n\n*I have always waited.*\n\n*The keyhole watches you like an eye. Through it, if you press close enough, you can see only darkness — and within that darkness, a single point of light, impossibly far away, that might be a room, might be a star, might be nothing at all.*\n\n*Do you have what fits?*"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":178,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}